# API structure (`apps/api/src/`)

Layers (boundaries enforced by lint in `.oxlintrc.json` — never violate):

- `lib/` — pure utility; imports NOTHING from the app
- `integrations/` — external service wrapper (openai, resend, r2); only uses `lib/`
- `db/` — client, `schema.ts` (barrel), columns, seed
- `domains/<d>/` — business: typically `schema.ts`, `repository.ts`, `service.ts`, `dto.ts`, `emails.ts`, `middleware.ts`, `routes/` (handlers + `index.ts` route map), `tools/` (tools + `index.ts` registry). Not every domain has every file — resource domains (`task`, `article`) are the full template; `account` is routes-only (HTTP for profile/password/API keys); `billing` has no schema/tools; `usage` tracks spend without HTTP routes
- **API keys ownership**: credentials live in `auth` (table `api_keys`, repository + `createApiKey`/`resolveApiKey` in auth service). Account owns the user-facing HTTP surface (`/api/account/api-keys` + `account/dto.ts`) and checks membership before minting. Do not duplicate the table under account — keys are auth credentials, account is the management UI.
- `agent/` — agent surface (not a domain); domains only import `@/agent/tool`. Agent-owned tools may live in `agent/tools/`
- `app.ts` builds routes; `server.ts` starts the server; `context.ts` = request types

Imports: `@/` alias for anything crossing a boundary; relative (`./`, `../`) only within the same domain.

Where to add:

- Route: `domains/<d>/routes/<action>.route.ts` → register in `routes/index.ts`
- Tool: `domains/<d>/tools/<action>.tool.ts` → register in `tools/index.ts` (and a new domain in `agent/registry.ts`)
- Table: schema in the domain → export in `db/schema.ts` → `db:generate`
- Env var: Zod schema in `lib/env.ts` + `.env.example` + `render.yaml` (when production needs it)
- Schema/DTO shared with web: `packages/shared/src/<domain>.ts`

Rules:

- Table shape (copy `domains/task/schema.ts`): `uuid("id").primaryKey().defaultRandom()`, `tenant_id` FK with `onDelete: "cascade"`, `...timestamps` from `@/db/columns`, and an index on `tenantId`. Same JSDoc habit as repositories: file header (title + module description), each table with title / blank / description; non-obvious columns get the same treatment.
- Route handler is `export async function <action>(c: AppContext)` — the name matches the route action (`createTask`, `login`), no `Route` suffix, no default export. Same JSDoc habit: title / blank / `` `METHOD /path` `` (final HTTP route) / blank / description / `@param c` / `@returns` (status + body).
- Route body uses three section banners (same dash length as existing handlers): `// -- Input -----------------------------------------------------------------`, `// -- Processing ------------------------------------------------------------`, `// -- Output ----------------------------------------------------------------`. Input holds `parseBody` / `uuidParam` / `c.get` and other request locals; Processing holds repository/service calls, auth checks, business rules and throws; Output holds DTO mapping, cookies and `c.json` / return. Always include all three, even on thin handlers. Blank line before each banner (except possibly Input right after `{`) and blank line between sections.
- Validate JSON bodies with `parseBody(c, schema)` (schema from `@app/shared`); read UUID route params with `uuidParam(c, "name")`; throw `HttpError(status, message)`; return with `c.json(...)`. Multipart uploads validate in-route.
- Map table rows to DTOs in `dto.ts` (`toXxxDto`), never inline inside a route or repository. Aggregate/snapshot DTOs (e.g. billing) may be assembled in `service.ts`. Same JSDoc habit as repositories: file header (title + module description), each export with title / blank / description / `@param` / `@returns`.
- All SQL lives in `repository.ts` as an exported object of async methods. Two shapes (copy the matching one):
  - **Resource repo** (canonical: `task`; also `article`): one primary table, tenant-scoped. Use the CRUD names you need (`list` / `find` / `insert` / `update` / `delete`) — article also has `updateCover`. Every method takes `tenantId` and filters by it. Write each query inline in the method (no shared query helpers). Mutations use `.returning()` when the row is needed. Annotate returns. File header is title + module description (official tone, not "template"). Each method: title, blank line, description, then `@param` / `@returns`. Prefer `/** */` over `//`.
  - **Platform repo** (`auth`, `tenant`, `usage`, `admin`): owns several tables or non-CRUD access. Prefix methods by entity (`insertUser`, `listMembers`, `sumUserTenantSpendSince`). Same JSDoc habit as resource repos. `billing` has no repository (catalog + service only).
- Repository returns DB rows / join shapes — never `@app/shared` DTOs. Map in `dto.ts` (or service for aggregates).
- `service.ts` only when there's real business logic; plain CRUD calls the repository straight from the route/tool. Same JSDoc habit as repositories: file header (title + module description), each export with title / blank / description / `@param` / `@returns`.
- Tenant route maps live in `routes/index.ts` (mirrors `tools/index.ts`): apply `requireAuth`/`requireTenant` once via `.use`, export the Hono group(s). Same JSDoc habit: file header (title + module description) and a title / blank / description on each exported route group (include mount path).
- Public, token-authenticated surfaces may be a second export from the same `routes/index.ts`, mounted at their own path — accepted exceptions: tenant `inviteRoutes` (`/api/invites`), platform `joinRoutes` (`/api/join`), and agent `mcpRoutes` (`/api/mcp`, API-key Bearer auth)
- Platform admin (`domains/admin/`): cross-tenant lists/edits only. Mount at `/api/admin` with `.use("*", requireAuth, requirePlatformAdmin)`. Never skip `requireTenant` on existing tenant resources as a shortcut — dedicated admin repos only. Effective admin = `users.isPlatformAdmin` OR verified email in `PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS` (orthogonal to tenant roles).
